7. Đối với chuyến bay thực hiện chương trình bay khai thác dưới sự giám sát để nâng hạng lái chính, sát hạch viên bay hoặc giáo viên huấn luyện bay đảm nhận vai trò người chỉ huy tàu bay. Sát hạch viên bay hoặc giáo viên huấn luyện bay được ngồi tại ghế quan sát sau khi người lái tàu bay đáp ứng các yêu cầu sau:
a) Đã thực hiện 02 lần cất cánh và hạ cánh trên loại tàu bay đó;
b) Được người giám sát đánh giá đủ khả năng thực hiện an toàn nhiệm vụ của lái chính.","isVerbatim":true,"translatedText":"Article 862. Regulations on flying under supervision for aircraft pilots

Article 862. Regulations on flying under supervision for aircraft pilots
1. The program of operating flights under supervision or flying to accumulate initial operational experience has the following objectives:
a) Help aircraft pilots become familiar with the actual operating environment of aircraft operators, including the entire operating process from flight preparation to flight completion at the apron;
b) Develop and evaluate capabilities for situational awareness, threat and error management, problem solving, and decision making in real-life mining environments;
c) Evaluate the ability to apply standard operating procedures, crew coordination and operational management in actual operating conditions.
2. After completing the training and testing course, the flight crew member performs a number of flight segments or operating flight hours under the supervision of a flight examiner, flight instructor or aircraft commander designated by the aircraft operator to perform the supervision task.
3. The number of flight segments or flight hours operated under supervision and with accumulated initial operating experience is specified in the aircraft operator's documentation system based on the following factors:
a) Previous experience of the pilot;
b) Complexity of the aircraft;
c) Type and scope of mining activities;
d) Results of training, testing and capacity assessment;
d) Position of the aircraft pilot.
4. Minimum requirements for operating under supervision and accumulating initial operating experience for aircraft with maximum takeoff weight greater than 5,700 kg or passenger seat configuration greater than 09 seats are as follows:
