5. Requirements for flying under supervision and accumulating initial operating experience for aircraft with a maximum takeoff weight of up to 5,700 kg or passenger seat configuration of up to 09 seats are as follows:
Subject: Minimum number of flight segments or flight hours Flight training pilots accumulate initial operating experience 50 flight segments or 100 flight hours, whichever comes first Aircraft pilot upgraded to primary pilot class 30 flight segments Airplane pilot with no operating experience in Vietnam and converted to a Vietnamese aircraft operator 05 flight segments Airplane pilot with experience in Vietnam operations and converted to aircraft operator 04 flight segments Airplane pilot with no operational experience operating in Vietnam switching to a new type of aircraft15 flight segments or 30 flight hours, whichever comes firstAirplane pilot with experience operating in Vietnam switching to a new aircraft type10 flight segments or 20 flight hours, whichever comes firstAirplane pilot resuming operations after a hiatus of more than 01 year05 flight segments or 10 flight hours, whichever comes firstAirplane pilot resuming operations after a period of interruption and must retrain the program Changing aircraft type 20 flight segments or 40 flight hours, whichever comes first Aircraft pilot reinstating rating 04 flight segments or 10 flight hours, whichever comes first
6. Aircraft operators develop a program to evaluate the flight operation process under supervision and accumulate initial flight experience to monitor, evaluate and confirm the actual operational capacity of the aircraft pilot.
7. For flights carrying out an operational flight program under supervision to upgrade the rank of chief pilot, the flight examiner or flight instructor assumes the role of aircraft commander. The flight examiner or flight instructor may sit in the observation chair after the pilot meets the following requirements:
