Article 878. Contents of periodic training program for aircraft pilots
1. Ground training includes the following contents:
a) Aircraft system;
b) Normal operating procedures, including flight planning, ground handling, flight operations, aircraft performance, weight and balance, fuel options, alternate airport selection, anti-icing and ground de-icing when applicable;
c) Abnormal and emergency procedures, including flight crew member incapacitation, when applicable;
d) Training contents related to safety, incidents, accidents or typical operational situations directly related to the type of aircraft;
d) Aviation security training;
e) Dangerous goods training;
g) Safety management system training;
h) Fatigue management training
i) Flight crew resource management training.
k) Ground training knowledge is tested and evaluated using appropriate methods.
2. Periodic training and inspection of emergency, safety and survival equipment for flight crew members is carried out on the aircraft or appropriate training equipment, combined with periodic inspection and includes the following contents:
a) Location, function and use of emergency, safety and survival equipment equipped on the aircraft;
b) Use emergency exit doors, means of escape and fire-fighting equipment;
c) Security procedures and handling of emergency situations;
d) Coordination between flight crew members and flight attendants or other flight crew members in emergency situations and first aid appropriate to the aircraft type, type of operation and flight crew composition when applicable;
d) For surface and offshore exploitation activities or other specific exploitation activities, training on water survival, escape and use of appropriate survival equipment;
e) Practice coordinating aircraft escapes and two-way communication between flight crew members in emergency situations;
g) The training cycle, mandatory practice content, water survival training, underwater escape training, inspection methods and other detailed technical requirements are specified in the aircraft operator's training program.
3. Train flight crew resource management to comply with the following requirements:
a) The content of flight crew resource management training is integrated into appropriate stages of the periodic training program for flight crew members;
b) Training in flight crew resource management appropriate to the type of aircraft, type of operation, operating environment and operational tasks of flight crew members.
4. Flight training on aircraft and simulator flight training equipment must comply with the following requirements:
a) The training program on aircraft and simulated flight training equipment is developed in accordance with the aircraft manufacturer's documents, ensuring that major failures of the aircraft system and related procedures are carried out in a training cycle of no more than 03 years;
b) When performing flight operations with an engine failure situation on the aircraft, the engine failure situation is performed in a hypothetical form;
c) Periodic training on aircraft and simulator flight training equipment for individual exercises or operations is separate from testing the capacity of the aircraft operator.
5. For helicopters, if there is suitable and available simulator flight training equipment, the simulator flight training equipment is used to complete the following contents:
a) Subsidence phenomenon has capacity and vortex state;
b) Unwanted rotation and loss of tail rotor efficiency.
6. For aircraft operations other than complex engine aircraft, training and inspection content is appropriate to the type of operation and class of aircraft that the crew member operates, and also takes into account the specialized equipment used.
7. Training in handling incapacity of flight crew members must comply with the following requirements:
a) Aircraft operators develop a 12-month theoretical training program on recognizing and handling the incapacity of flight crew members;
b) Training to recognize the incapacity to work of flight crew members is carried out in the form of focused training, discussion or audio-visual presentation;
c) Practical training on handling incapacity of flight crew members is carried out on simulators, aircraft or appropriate training vehicles with a cycle of no more than 03 years.","translations":{"en":"Article 878. Contents of periodic training program for aircraft pilots

