Article 880. Periodic training for air mechanics and air navigation
1. The aircraft operator must ensure that the flight engineer or air navigator completes periodic training every 12 months according to the aircraft operator's training program.
2. Aircraft operators ensuring air mechanics or air navigation complete a periodic 12-month ground training program on the following contents:
a) Aviation security training;
b) Dangerous goods training;
c) Safety management system training;
d) Fatigue management training
d) Training in flight crew resource management.
