Article 906. Initial training program for flight attendant inspection teachers
1. Aircraft operators develop a training program to ensure that instructors checking flight attendants complete the initial training program specified in the operating manual before performing their duties.
2. The initial training program includes a minimum duration of 08 hours, including the following contents:
No. Knowledge/SkillsContent 1General knowledge - Training on document systems and current legal documents.- Standard operating procedures (SOP).- Safety management system (SMS), hazard identification from training results.- Knowledge about aircraft types.2Evaluation and scoring skills- Evidence-based training and testing skills- How to apply the evaluation scale.- Understanding of the evaluation process.- Observational skills Observe, record errors and evaluate students' level of satisfaction. - Analyze students' strengths and weaknesses, including feedback from students. - Distinguish between objectivity and subjectivity. - Standardize assessment skills. 3Human factors & Flight crew resource management - Methods to evaluate team coordination and communication skills of flight attendants. 4Operating training equipment - How to operate training equipment safely. - Ensuring all assessment activities takes place in safe conditions.5Debriefing Skills - How to give constructive feedback for students to self-aware and overcome.6Inspection and reporting process - Recording assessment - Post-assessment reporting","translations":{"en":"Article 906. Initial training program for flight attendant inspection teachers

