Article 909. Main driver upgrade training program
1. The main pilot upgrade training program for aircraft operators applies to the following cases:
a) Co-pilot is upgraded to main pilot on the same type of aircraft, without changing the assigned aircraft type rating;
b) Co-pilot is upgraded to main pilot combined with changing aircraft type.
2. Aircraft pilots participating in the main pilot upgrade training program of aircraft operators must meet the following requirements:
a) Have a valid airline transport pilot's license with the corresponding aircraft type rating issued or recognized by the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam;
b) Meet the standards and procedures for selecting and upgrading chief pilots of aircraft operators;
c) In the case of upgrading the main pilot combined with changing the aircraft type, the pilot completes the training program to change the aircraft type as prescribed in the training program before performing the training to upgrade the main pilot.
3. The main pilot upgrade training program for aircraft complies with the following requirements:
a) The main pilot upgrade training program includes 03 stages: ground training, training on a flight simulator and operational flight under supervision, ending with an operational check on the flight line;
b) Ground training includes the following contents:
Subjects Training content Minimum duration Responsibilities and obligations of the main pilot Responsibilities and obligations of the main pilot according to the provisions of Vietnamese law on civil aviation; Certificate of aircraft operator and scope of operations; regulations and procedures on aircraft techniques and aircraft operations for main pilots; decision making and risk management in mining; responsibility for management, command and coordination with flight attendants, flight operations dispatchers, maintenance staff, ground staff and other related personnel.08 hoursHuman factors and flight crew resource managementPersonal awareness, human error and human reliability; attitudes, behavior, self-assessment, self-criticism and learning from experience; managing pressure in aircraft operations; fatigue management; situational awareness, information gathering and processing; use and manage aircraft automation systems; solve problems and make decisions.08 hours Aviation security for the main pilot. Responsibilities of the main pilot according to the provisions of Vietnamese law on aviation security; handle illegal interference and disruptive behavior; cockpit security check procedures and cockpit door protection; Handling reports of bombs and suspicious items and searching for bombs on aircraft. 06 hours
c) Training on simulated flight training equipment includes the following contents:
Category Training content Management of normal, abnormal and emergency situations Exploitation in adverse weather conditions; abnormal and emergency procedures of the aircraft type; diversion flights and alternate airports; mining in metric units; abort takeoff; post-takeoff engine failure, including engine failure between V1 and V2 and single engine operation; approach and landing under abnormal flight control conditions or impaired flight protection; in-flight fuel management, minimum fuel status and emergency fuel status; manage fire, smoke, and toxic odor situations during flights; re-flight procedures with different power levels and re-entry altitudes, including aborting landings. Flight training according to actual operating scenarios. Performing flights according to the actual flight path of the aircraft operator; The training scenario is not announced to the flight crew in advance to ensure effective training for surprise and startle effects; Coordination process with flight attendants and air traffic service providers. Final competency assessment Comprehensive assessment of main pilot competency according to the applicable competency framework; The test scenario is not announced to the flight crew in advance to ensure effective assessment of unexpected effects; The final test on a simulated flight training device to evaluate the completion of the main pilot upgrade training program is integrated with the type rating test when applicable and is performed by a flight examiner of the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam. Operation in low visibility conditions and zero flight time training when applicable Takeoff and landing procedures in limited visibility conditions; circling and visual approaches on a simulated flight training device. Avoidance and recovery of abnormal postures Flying in normal and reduced protection modes, including at low and high altitudes; flight automation system management, including disconnection, reconnection, and failure handling; aircraft energy management; recognize and recover from abnormal aircraft attitudes; recovery from a stall situation. The number of training exercises on a simulated flight training device is determined by the aircraft operator in the training program, including a minimum of 05 training exercises, excluding training exercises for special forms of operations, air-time training and competency assessment tests.
d) After meeting the requirements of the training phase on the simulator flight training device, the pilot of the aircraft shall perform flight operations under supervision and inspection of operations on the flight path according to the following requirements:
Phase Required to fly under supervision Number of flight segments determined by the aircraft operator in the training program but not less than 60 flight segments under supervision; performed in the left seat position as the main pilot under the supervision of a flight examiner or flight instructor; Carry out all duties and responsibilities of the main pilot during flights under supervision. Operational inspection on the flight route at the end of the program is performed by flight examiners of the Vietnam Aviation Administration; Comprehensive assessment of capacity according to the capacity framework of aircraft pilots and standards applicable to main pilots of aircraft operators.
4. The main pilot upgrade training program for helicopters complies with the following requirements:
a) The main pilot upgrade training program includes 03 stages: ground training, training on a flight simulator or on an aircraft and operating under supervision, ending with an operational check on the flight line;
b) Ground training includes the following contents:
