Article 920. Regulations on circadian rhythm synchronization state
The state of circadian rhythm synchronization is determined based on the difference between the triple reference time and the local time. When the local time at the starting place of a mission differs more than 2 hours from the local time at the starting place of the next mission, for the purpose of calculating the maximum daily flight duty period, the flight crew member is considered to be in a state of synchronized circadian rhythm corresponding to the prescribed values as follows:
