3. In case the FDP is extended due to in-flight rest time, in-flight rest equipment must meet the following standards:
a) Type 1 resting equipment: Bed or flat or nearly flat surface that allows the flight crew to sleep and recline at least 80 degrees, arranged in an area separate from the cockpit and passenger compartment, controlled by temperature, lighting, and soundproofing;
b) Type 2 rest equipment: Seats in the passenger compartment can recline at least 45 degrees, have a distance between two rows of seats of at least 137.5cm, seats are at least 50cm wide, have footrests, are arranged in an area separated from passengers by at least a curtain to block light and minimize noise, and not be disturbed by passengers or flight crew members;
c) Type 3 resting equipment: seats in the passenger compartment or cockpit have a leg rest support and are separated from the passenger area by at least a curtain to block light and minimize noise, not next to any occupied passenger seat.
4. The application of extended FDP, with rest time on the flight must comply with the following regulations:
a) No more than 03 stages for 01 FDP;
b) The minimum in-flight rest time is not less than 90 consecutive minutes for each flight crew member and 02 consecutive hours for the flight crew member controlling the aircraft during the landing phase.
5. In case an extension of the maximum daily FDP is applied due to in-flight rest, the maximum FDP is specified as follows:
a) For 01 additional crew member, the maximum FDP must not exceed 14 hours with rest equipment type 03, 15 hours with rest equipment type 02, 16 hours with rest equipment type 01;
b) For 02 additional crew members, the maximum FDP must not exceed 15 hours with rest equipment type 03, 16 hours with rest equipment type 02, 17 hours with rest equipment type 01.
