3. The maximum total flight time within 07 days must not exceed 30 hours when there are 05 consecutive FDPs during the period from 02:00 - 06:00 (local time).
4. Flight duty time includes the time to perform pre-flight and post-flight preparation tasks according to regulations of the aircraft operator with the minimum time for pre-flight preparation tasks being 30 minutes and for post-flight duties being 15 minutes.
5. Flight crew members performing multiple flight operations must be given at least one mid-shift meal break of no less than 60 minutes in case the flight duty time is 6 hours or more.
6. Flight crew members wearing survival suits shall not engage in the movement of cargo, baggage or any other activity requiring undue physical exertion.
7. In case the flight duty time exceeds 04 hours and 30 minutes, the minimum rest time is 30 minutes, excluding a total of 30 minutes for pre- and post-flight duties. This rest period must be scheduled before flight time exceeds 6 hours.
8. In unforeseen situations, the aircraft commander may extend the flight duty time up to 02 hours provided that the flight time and duty time are not exceeded.
9. The maximum number of times allowed to extend flight duty time is no more than 02 times in any period of 07 consecutive days.
10. After the flight duty time is extended, the aircraft commander must report to the aircraft operator.
11. In case the flight duty time is extended for more than 02 hours or when the flight duty time is extended or the extension is carried out after applying a shortened minimum rest time, the aircraft operator must submit a copy of the aircraft commander's report attached with the aircraft operator's assessment to the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam no later than 28 days after the incident occurred.","translations":{"en":"Article 947. Maximum flight time and duty time

