8. Quy trình bất thường và quy trình dự phòng đối với RNAV 5 phải bao gồm việc xử lý mất hoặc suy giảm nguồn tín hiệu dẫn đường, sai lệch đường bay vượt giới hạn, dữ liệu điểm đường bay bị nhập sai, thiết bị dẫn đường mặt đất cần thiết không hoạt động hoặc mất khả năng đáp ứng RNAV 5.","isVerbatim":true,"translatedText":"Article 1046. Requirements for RNAV exploitation 5

Article 1046. Requirements for RNAV exploitation 5
1. RNAV 5 operations are carried out in the airspace, flight path or flight phase announced to apply RNAV 5.
2. The navigation system used for RNAV 5 uses navigation signal sources from the inertial navigation system, global navigation satellite system, DME/DME, VOR/DME or a combination of these navigation signal sources when appropriate to the aircraft configuration, navigation infrastructure and published operating conditions.
3. Operational instructions documents must clearly specify the navigation signal source used to meet RNAV 5 for each type of aircraft, each system configuration and each operating area.
4. Before performing a flight in the airspace or route where RNAV 5 is applied, flight crew members are responsible for checking the status of the navigation system, navigation signal source, minimum equipment list, aeronautical information information file, aeronautical information notice, navigation infrastructure and flight plan in the aircraft system.
5. Where RNAV 5 is performed by manual entry of route point data, the operating procedure must provide for independent cross-checking of route point coordinates, route point order, track, distance, azimuth and displayed route before use.
6. Manual entry of route point data for RNAV 5 must not be performed during high-workload flight periods or under conditions that do not ensure independent cross-checking.
7. RNAV 5 operational procedures must provide for checking gross errors using conventional navigation equipment, independent navigation systems or other suitable methods when required by operational conditions.
8. Abnormal procedures and contingency procedures for RNAV 5 should include addressing loss or degradation of navigation signal sources, out-of-bounds route deviations, incorrectly entered route point data, failure of essential ground navigation equipment, or loss of ability to respond to RNAV 5.","translations":{"en":"Article 1046. Requirements for RNAV exploitation 5

