Article 1052. Requirements for RNP 0.3 helicopter operations
1. RNP 0.3 operations are carried out for helicopters on routes, airspace, standard instrument departure procedures, standard instrument arrival procedures, instrument approach procedures, reentry phases or announced operating areas applying RNP 0.3.
2. The navigation system used for RNP 0.3 must use the global navigation satellite system as the main source of navigation signals, in accordance with the flight manual or technical documents issued by the organization responsible for designing the aircraft type.
3. Navigation systems used for RNP 0.3 must not use DME/DME as the sole basis for meeting RNP 0.3 standards.
4. The navigation system used for RNP 0.3 must have the function of monitoring and warning the aircraft's navigation features in accordance with the RNP 0.3 value.
5. Routes, standard instrument departure procedures, standard instrument arrival procedures, instrument approach procedures or re-flight phases applying RNP 0.3 must be loaded from a valid navigation database, except in cases where route construction using route points from a published navigation database and is permitted by the operations manual.
6. Before performing RNP 0.3 operations, flight crew members are responsible for checking the helicopter, navigation system, navigation satellite signal source, navigation database, aeronautical information information file, aeronautical information announcement, airspace conditions, meteorological conditions, terrain, obstacles, helipads, take-off and landing sites, operation areas and related backup plans.
7. RNP 0.3 operations procedures must consider helicopter operations characteristics, including low flight speeds, low flight altitudes, terrain, obstacles, restricted operations areas, operations to or from heliports, take-off and landing sites, and offshore operations areas when applicable.
8. Abnormal procedures and contingency procedures for RNP 0.3 must include handling loss or deterioration of the global navigation satellite system, RNP non-response alerts, excessive route deviations, inadequate navigation databases, display systems or flight guidance systems that are no longer operating properly, inadequate clearances by air traffic service providers, inappropriate meteorological conditions, terrain, obstacles or operating areas. to continue executing the method.","translations":{"en":"Article 1052. Requirements for RNP 0.3 helicopter operations

