a) According to the criteria specified in the aircraft's flight manual for expected weather conditions;
b) In case the aircraft's flight manual does not specify, it is determined by reducing the value of runway visibility or the converted visibility level applicable to operations that do not use the enhanced vision support system when flying or the combined vision system.
3. The value of runway visibility or converted visibility level for operations using an enhanced vision support system in flight or a combined vision system, compared to the required value when not using this system, is determined as follows:
Runway visibility value or transitional visibility level required when not using enhanced vision aids in flight Runway visibility value or required transitional visibility level when using enhanced vision aids while flying550 m350 m600 m400 m650 m450 m700 m450 m750 m500 m800 m550 m900 m600 m1,000 m650 m1,100 m750 m1,200 m800 m1,300 m900 m1,400 m900 m1,500 m1,000 m1,600 m1,100 m1,700 m1,100 m1,800 m1,200 m1,900 m1,300 m2,000 m1,300 m2,100 m1,400 m2,200 m1,500 m2,300 m1,500 m2,400 m1,600 m
