Article 1151. Meteorological conditions
1. Helicopter commanders shall only perform flights according to visual flight rules between offshore locations located in Class G airspace when the flight segment over water does not exceed 10 NM and meteorological conditions are equal to or better than the minimum standard according to the number of pilots and time of operation as determined as follows:
Minimum standardsDaytimeNight01 riderHeight: 300 ft Visibility: 3 kmHeight: 500 ft Visibility: 5 kmTwo ridersHeight: 300 ft Visibility: 2 kmHeight: 500 ft Visibility: 5 km
2. The cloud bottom must ensure that the helicopter can maintain flight at the specified height without flying into the clouds.
3. For single-pilot operations during the day, helicopter operations are permitted with reduced visibility down to 800 m when the destination or intermediate structure can be continuously seen.
4. For two-man operations at night, helicopter operations are permitted with reduced visibility down to 1,500 m when the destination or intermediate structure is continuously visible.","translations":{"en":"Article 1151. Meteorological conditions

