Article 1166. The crew operates a winch crane operation by helicopter
1. Aircraft operators are responsible for developing criteria for selecting flight crew members to perform helicopter winch operations, taking into account previous operating experience appropriate to the type of task and operating environment.
2. The helicopter commander performing the task of operating a winch by helicopter offshore must meet the following experience requirements:
a) Have a minimum of 750 flight hours as a helicopter commander or 750 flight hours as a co-pilot in helicopter winch operations, including a minimum of 200 hours as a helicopter commander under supervision;
b) Complete at least 10 winching cycles at sea, including at least 03 winching cycles at night if performing night operations.
3. The helicopter commander performing the task of operating a winch by helicopter on land must meet the following experience requirements:
a) Have a minimum of 500 flight hours as a helicopter commander or 500 flight hours as a co-pilot in helicopter winch operations, including a minimum of 100 hours as a helicopter commander under supervision;
b) Have at least 200 hours of helicopter operating experience in an operating environment with similar geographical characteristics to the expected operating activities;
c) Complete a minimum of 30 winching cycles, including a minimum of 10 winching cycles at night if night operations are performed.
4. A helicopter winch operation mission may include multiple winch cycles; One winch cycle is counted as one down and up of the hook.
5. Crew members participating in helicopter crane operations are responsible for completing the training course in accordance with the procedures specified in the operation manual and meeting the experience requirements appropriate to the role and expected operating environment.
6. Crew members participating in helicopter crane operations are responsible for completing within the previous 180 days:
a) For daytime operations, a minimum of three helicopter winching cycles during the day or at night, each mission including a minimum of one transition to and from the hovering condition;
b) For night operations, a minimum of three nighttime helicopter winching cycles, each mission including a minimum of one transition to and from the hangover condition.
7. The aircraft operator is responsible for specifying the minimum flight crew composition for helicopter crane operations in the operating manual, taking into account the type of helicopter, meteorological conditions, type of mission and, for offshore operations, the environment at the location of the operation, sea state and movement of vessels.
8. The minimum flight crew includes one pilot and one technical flight crew member operating winch crane operations by helicopter. Technical flight crew member is a flight crew member assigned by the aircraft operator to perform tasks on the aircraft or on the ground to support the pilot in helicopter hoist operations, including operating specialized equipment on the aircraft.","translations":{"en":"Article 1166. The crew operates a winch crane operation by helicopter

