5. Gia hạn Giấy chứng nhận đủ điều kiện bay và Giấy chứng nhận lắp đặt thiết bị vô tuyến điện tàu bay được Giám sát viên an toàn ký xác nhận thời hạn hiệu lực vào mặt sau của Giấy chứng nhận sau khi Cục Hàng không Việt Nam ban hành quyết định gia hạn.","isVerbatim":true,"translatedText":"Article 1174. Procedures for issuance, re-issuance, amendment, extension and recognition of Certificate of airworthiness

Article 1174. Procedures for issuance, re-issuance, amendment, extension and recognition of Certificate of airworthiness
1. Submit and receive documents:
a) The applicant for issuance, re-issuance, modification, extension or recognition of the Certificate of airworthiness shall submit 01 set of documents through the National Public Service Portal, via postal service or directly at the One-Stop Department of the Vietnam Aviation Administration;
b) Dossier requesting issuance, re-issuance, amendment, extension, and recognition of the Certificate of airworthiness includes the documents specified in Article 1173 of these Regulations. For an extension application, the applicant must submit the application at least 60 days before the expiration date of the Certificate of airworthiness;
c) Within 01 working day from the date of receiving the dossier, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam checks the accuracy and completeness of the dossier. In case the application is in accordance with regulations, the application will be received and notified of fee payment; In case the dossier is not complete as prescribed, the notice will instruct the applicant to supplement and complete the dossier;
d) Within 05 working days from the date of notice of fee payment, the applicant is responsible for completing the obligation to pay fees and charges. In case the applicant does not fulfill the obligation to pay fees and charges, the Vietnam Aviation Administration refuses to handle administrative procedures. The applicant's time to pay fees and charges is not included in the time to resolve administrative procedures.
2. Carry out procedures for issuance, extension, and recognition of Certificate of airworthiness, except for the case of granting a special Certificate of airworthiness in the form of a special flight permit:
a) Within 15 working days from the date of receipt of complete documents as prescribed and the applicant completes the obligation to pay fees and charges, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam shall evaluate the aircraft documents according to the provisions of Article 1175 of these Regulations and check the technical condition of the aircraft when necessary;
b) In case the inspection results detect non-conformities, within 02 working days from the date of completion of the inspection, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam shall notify in writing or electronically requesting the applicant to correct the problem. The time the requester takes to make the correction is not included in the time limit for resolving administrative procedures. The time limit for resolving administrative procedures is continued from the date the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam receives the remediation report and determines that the remediation is satisfactory.
Within 30 days from the date of receiving the request for remediation, if the requester does not submit a remediation report or the remediation does not meet the requirements, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam shall notify in writing or in the electronic environment the termination of the procedure; Paid fees and charges are non-refundable.
c) Within 03 working days from the end of the inspection of the aircraft, no non-conformities are detected or from the date of confirmation of satisfactory remediation, the Vietnam Aviation Administration shall issue a decision to issue, extend and recognize the Certificate of airworthiness along with the Certificate of installation of radio equipment on the aircraft.
3. Carry out re-issuance procedures:
a) In case of re-issuance due to expiration: the order and procedures shall comply with the provisions of Clause 2 of this Article;
b) In case of re-issuance due to loss, damage or modification at the request of the applicant: within 03 working days from the date of receipt of complete documents as prescribed, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam shall issue a decision to re-issue or amend the Certificate of airworthiness, and at the same time revoke the issued Certificate, except in cases where the certificate is lost;
c) In case of re-issuance due to the results of inspection, supervision or assessment of the airworthiness of the aircraft requiring amendment of the Certificate of airworthiness, the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam shall amend the Certificate of airworthiness within 03 working days after evaluating the records, documents and actual condition of the aircraft; If necessary, request the owner, lessee or operator of the aircraft to provide records and documents or take corrective measures and update information.
4. Issuing a Certificate of special airworthiness in the form of a special flight permit: within 03 working days from the date of receiving complete documents as prescribed, the Vietnam Aviation Administration decides to issue a Certificate of special airworthiness to the applicant.
5. Renewing the Certificate of airworthiness and the Certificate of installation of aircraft radio equipment must be signed by the Safety Supervisor to confirm the validity period on the back of the Certificate after the Civil Aviation Authority of Vietnam issues the decision to extend.","translations":{"en":"Article 1174. Procedures for issuance, re-issuance, amendment, extension and recognition of Certificate of airworthiness

