Article 1238. Training and testing for flight attendants
1. When performing their duties, flight attendants must complete initial training as prescribed in Part VII of these Regulations.
2. The training course must include theoretical and practical instruction, along with individual or group practice appropriate to each training component, to ensure that flight attendants achieve and maintain an appropriate level of proficiency as required by this Part.
3. Aircraft operator conversion training program and aircraft type conversion training program include:
a) Cabin crew members must complete the appropriate training course for each specific aircraft type and the aircraft operator's conversion training course, along with related tests before: being assigned by the aircraft operator to perform flight attendant duties for the first time or being assigned by the aircraft operator to operate on another type of aircraft;
b) When developing training programs and textbooks for specific aircraft types and type conversion training, operators must include the contents specified in the mandatory section of operational appropriate data or equivalent documents issued by the aircraft manufacturing organization;
c) The training program for the specific aircraft type must include training and practice on simulators or on actual aircraft;
d) The training program for specific aircraft types and type conversion training of aircraft operators must include knowledge about aircraft, passenger cabin configuration, safety and emergency equipment; operate doors, emergency exits, escape slides and systems related to handling emergency situations and crew incapacitation; Normal operating procedures, emergency, fire fighting, passenger escape, passenger control.
4. Train aircraft differences
a) Cabin crew members must complete appropriate differences training and testing before being assigned to operate on: a variant of the type of aircraft being operated or a type or variant of aircraft being operated that has differences in safety equipment, location of safety and emergency equipment, or normal and emergency operations procedures;
b) The different training program must be determined on the basis of comparison with the training program that cabin crew members have completed in aircraft type change training and aircraft operator change training according to the provisions of Clause 3 of this Article for the relevant aircraft type and includes training and practice on simulated training equipment or on actual aircraft in accordance with the different content that needs to be trained;
c) When developing a differentiated training program and curriculum for a variant of the aircraft type in operation, the operator must include, when applicable, the relevant contents specified in the mandatory section of the operational suitability data or equivalent documents issued by the aircraft manufacturing organization.
5. After completing aircraft type change training and aircraft operator change training for a type of aircraft, flight attendants must complete familiarization training and fly familiarization on that type of aircraft before being assigned operational duties.
6. Periodic training
a) Each flight attendant must complete annual training and testing;
b) Periodic training must include the tasks assigned to each flight attendant in normal and emergency procedures and drills, appropriate to each aircraft type or aircraft variant being operated.
7. Recovery training
a) Ground recovery training and capacity testing on skills and emergency handling for aircraft types expected to be assigned tasks in case of interruption of more than 6 months on all types of aircraft in operation and the periodic training period is still valid from the time of performing the task on the most recent flight;
b) Rehabilitation training and capacity testing or completing at least 01 familiarization flight and 02 flights under supervision for the interrupted aircraft type in case the interruption period is more than 06 months on one of the operated aircraft types and the periodic training period is still valid from the time of performing duties on the most recent flight;
c) Complete the aircraft type conversion training program and aircraft operator conversion training program in case of interruption exceeding 12 months and less than 36 months;
d) Complete the initial flight attendant training program, aircraft type conversion training, and aircraft operator conversion training in case of interruption of more than 36 months.
8. After completing the training courses specified in this Article, flight attendants must complete a competency test by appropriately qualified personnel of the aircraft operator or cabin safety supervisor.","translations":{"en":"Article 1238. Training and testing for flight attendants

Article 1238. Training and testing for flight attendants
1. When performing their duties, flight attendants must complete initial training as prescribed in Part VII of these Regulations.
2. The training course must include theoretical and practical instruction, along with individual or group practice appropriate to each training component, to ensure that flight attendants achieve and maintain an appropriate level of proficiency as required by this Part.
3. Aircraft operator conversion training program and aircraft type conversion training program include:
a) Cabin crew members must complete the appropriate training course for each specific aircraft type and the aircraft operator's conversion training course, along with related tests before: being assigned by the aircraft operator to perform flight attendant duties for the first time or being assigned by the aircraft operator to operate on another type of aircraft;
b) When developing training programs and textbooks for specific aircraft types and type conversion training, operators must include the contents specified in the mandatory section of operational appropriate data or equivalent documents issued by the aircraft manufacturing organization;
c) The training program for the specific aircraft type must include training and practice on simulators or on actual aircraft;
d) The training program for specific aircraft types and type conversion training of aircraft operators must include knowledge about aircraft, passenger cabin configuration, safety and emergency equipment; operate doors, emergency exits, escape slides and systems related to handling emergency situations and crew incapacitation; Normal operating procedures, emergency, fire fighting, passenger escape, passenger control.
4. Train aircraft differences
a) Cabin crew members must complete appropriate differences training and testing before being assigned to operate on: a variant of the type of aircraft being operated or a type or variant of aircraft being operated that has differences in safety equipment, location of safety and emergency equipment, or normal and emergency operations procedures;
b) The different training program must be determined on the basis of comparison with the training program that cabin crew members have completed in aircraft type change training and aircraft operator change training according to the provisions of Clause 3 of this Article for the relevant aircraft type and includes training and practice on simulated training equipment or on actual aircraft in accordance with the different content that needs to be trained;
c) When developing a differentiated training program and curriculum for a variant of the aircraft type in operation, the operator must include, when applicable, the relevant contents specified in the mandatory section of the operational suitability data or equivalent documents issued by the aircraft manufacturing organization.
5. After completing aircraft type change training and aircraft operator change training for a type of aircraft, flight attendants must complete familiarization training and fly familiarization on that type of aircraft before being assigned operational duties.
6. Periodic training
a) Each flight attendant must complete annual training and testing;
b) Periodic training must include the tasks assigned to each flight attendant in normal and emergency procedures and drills, appropriate to each aircraft type or aircraft variant being operated.
7. Recovery training
a) Ground recovery training and capacity testing on skills and emergency handling for aircraft types expected to be assigned tasks in case of interruption of more than 6 months on all types of aircraft in operation and the periodic training period is still valid from the time of performing the task on the most recent flight;
b) Rehabilitation training and capacity testing or completing at least 01 familiarization flight and 02 flights under supervision for the interrupted aircraft type in case the interruption period is more than 06 months on one of the operated aircraft types and the periodic training period is still valid from the time of performing duties on the most recent flight;
c) Complete the aircraft type conversion training program and aircraft operator conversion training program in case of interruption exceeding 12 months and less than 36 months;
d) Complete the initial flight attendant training program, aircraft type conversion training, and aircraft operator conversion training in case of interruption of more than 36 months.
8. After completing the training courses specified in this Article, flight attendants must complete a competency test by appropriately qualified personnel of the aircraft operator or cabin safety supervisor."}},"1239":{"id":1239,"title":"Điều 1239. Thời hạn hiệu lực của đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện và kiểm tra định kỳ","chapter":"Chương II - KHAI THÁC HÀNG KHÔNG CHUNG: MÁY BAY LỚN, MÁY BAY TRANG BỊ ĐỘNG CƠ TUABIN PHẢN LỰC","partTitle":"Phần XXIII - HÀNG KHÔNG CHUNG ĐỐI VỚI","partId":"main_p_23","htmlContent":"<h1>Điều 1239. Thời hạn hiệu lực của đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện và kiểm tra định kỳ </h1><p>1. Trường hợp việc đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện và kiểm tra định kỳ được hoàn thành trong tháng hết hạn hiệu lực hoặc trong vòng 03 tháng cuối cùng trước khi hết thời hạn hiệu lực, thì thời hạn hiệu lực mới được tính kể từ ngày hết hạn hiệu lực ban đầu;</p><p>2. Trường hợp việc đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện hoặc kiểm tra được hoàn thành trước thời điểm 03 tháng cuối cùng của thời hạn hiệu lực, thì thời hạn hiệu lực mới được tính kể từ ngày cuối cùng của tháng mà việc huấn luyện hoặc kiểm tra được hoàn thành.</p>","plainText":"Điều 1239. Thời hạn hiệu lực của đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện và kiểm tra định kỳ
1. Trường hợp việc đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện và kiểm tra định kỳ được hoàn thành trong tháng hết hạn hiệu lực hoặc trong vòng 03 tháng cuối cùng trước khi hết thời hạn hiệu lực, thì thời hạn hiệu lực mới được tính kể từ ngày hết hạn hiệu lực ban đầu;
2. Trường hợp việc đánh giá kinh nghiệm hiện tại, huấn luyện hoặc kiểm tra được hoàn thành trước thời điểm 03 tháng cuối cùng của thời hạn hiệu lực, thì thời hạn hiệu lực mới được tính kể từ ngày cuối cùng của tháng mà việc huấn luyện hoặc kiểm tra được hoàn thành.","isVerbatim":true,"translatedText":"Article 1239. Validity period of current experience evaluation, training and periodic inspection

Article 1239. Validity period of current experience evaluation, training and periodic inspection
1. In case the evaluation of current experience, training and periodic inspection is completed within the month of expiration or within the last 03 months before the expiration of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the original validity expiration date;
2. In case the evaluation of current experience, training or testing is completed before the last 3 months of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the last day of the month in which the training or testing is completed.","translations":{"en":"Article 1239. Validity period of current experience evaluation, training and periodic inspection

Article 1239. Validity period of current experience evaluation, training and periodic inspection
1. In case the evaluation of current experience, training and periodic inspection is completed within the month of expiration or within the last 03 months before the expiration of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the original validity expiration date;
2. In case the evaluation of current experience, training or testing is completed before the last 3 months of the validity period, the new validity period is calculated from the last day of the month in which the training or testing is completed."}}},"parts":[{"id":"main_p_1","title":"Phần I - QUY ĐỊNH CHUNG","start":1,"end":27,"cat":"Phần I - QUY ĐỊNH CHUNG"},{"id":"main_p_2","title":"Phần II - ĐĂNG KÝ QUỐC TỊCH TÀU BAY","start":28,"end":32,"cat":"Phần II - ĐĂNG KÝ QUỐC TỊCH TÀU BAY"},{"id":"main_p_3","title":"Phần III - GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN LOẠI, GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN LOẠI BỔ SUNG, GIẤY XÁC NHẬN PHÙ HỢP TIÊU CHUẨN KỸ THUẬT, SỬA CHỮA ĐỐI VỚI TÀU BAY, ĐỘNG CƠ TÀU BAY VÀ CÁNH QUẠT TÀU BAY","start":33,"end":83,"cat":"Phần III - GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN LOẠI, GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN LOẠI BỔ SUNG, GIẤY XÁC NHẬN PHÙ HỢP TIÊU CHUẨN KỸ THUẬT, SỬA CHỮA ĐỐI VỚI TÀU BAY, ĐỘNG CƠ TÀU BAY VÀ CÁNH QUẠT TÀU BAY"},{"id":"main_p_4","title":"Phần IV - TIÊU CHUẨN ĐỦ ĐIỀU KIỆN BAY","start":84,"end":136,"cat":"Phần IV - TIÊU CHUẨN ĐỦ ĐIỀU KIỆN BAY"},{"id":"main_p_5","title":"Phần V - TỔ CHỨC BẢO DƯỠNG","start":137,"end":146,"cat":"Phần V - TỔ CHỨC BẢO DƯỠNG"},{"id":"main_p_6","title":"Phần VI - QUY ĐỊNH VỀ TRANG THIẾT BỊ TÀU BAY","start":147,"end":289,"cat":"Phần VI - QUY ĐỊNH VỀ TRANG THIẾT BỊ TÀU BAY"},{"id":"main_p_7","title":"Phần VII - NHÂN VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG","start":290,"end":474,"cat":"Phần VII - NHÂN VIÊN HÀNG KHÔNG"},{"id":"main_p_8","title":"Phần VIII - GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN SỨC KHỎE VÀ CƠ SỞ Y TẾ KHÁM SỨC KHỎE","start":475,"end":493,"cat":"Phần VIII - GIẤY CHỨNG NHẬN SỨC KHỎE VÀ CƠ SỞ Y TẾ KHÁM SỨC KHỎE"},{"id":"main_p_9","title":"Phần IX - CƠ SỞ ĐỦ ĐIỀU KIỆN ĐÀO TẠO, HUẤN LUYỆN NGHIỆP VỤ HUẤN LUYỆN HÀNG KHÔNG","start":494,"end":535,"cat":"Phần IX - CƠ SỞ ĐỦ ĐIỀU KIỆN ĐÀO TẠO, HUẤN LUYỆN NGHIỆP VỤ HUẤN LUYỆN HÀNG KHÔNG"},{"id":"main_p_10","title":"Phần X - KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY","start":536,"end":673,"cat":"Phần X - KHAI THÁC TÀU BAY"},{"id":"main_p_11","title":"Phần XI - HÀNG KHÔNG CHUYÊN DÙNG","start":674,"end":